          %title Reduced phase space
          %h2#ReducedPhaseSpace Reduced phase space
          %p In this chapter we discuss these topics:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Global gauge reduction for strictly
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
                functions (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functionals"}> action functionals
                ):
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "#DerivedCriticalLocusInsideLieAlgebroids"} Derived critical loci inside Lie algebroids
                %li
                  %p
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "#SchoutenBracketAntibracket"} Schouten bracket on Lie algebroids
            %li
              %p
                Local gauge reduction for weakly invariant local functions (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+densities"}> Lagrangian densities
                ):
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "#LocalJetBundleAntibracket"} Local antibracket
                %li
                  %p
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "#DerivedCriticalLocusOnJetBundle"} Local BV-BRST complex
                %li
                  %p
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "#BVBRSTComplexGlobal"} Global BV-BRST complex
          %p
            For a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+phase+space"} reduced phase space
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
            (the
            = succeed "-locus" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solution"} solution
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+symmetries"} gauge symmetries
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+symmetries"} gauge symmetries
            and its
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+intersection"} homotopy intersection
            with the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+phase+space"} reduced phase space
            may lift the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            to have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            and hence a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotients"} homotopy quotients
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+intersections"} homotopy intersections
            is usefully modeled by tools from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
          %p
            In order to exhibit the key structure without getting distracted by the local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
            geometry, we first discuss the simple form in which the reduced phase space would appear after
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression+of+variational+differential+forms"} transgression
            (def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TransgressionOfVariationalDifferentialFormsToConfigrationSpaces"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            were
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+extremal+action"} principle of extremal action
            (prop.
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PrincipleOfExtremalAction"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+critical+locus"} derived critical locus
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mi S
                  %mo ≃
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d S \simeq 0
            ) of a globally defined
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
            is example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ArchetypeOfBVBRSTComplex"}
            below.
          %p
            The genuine
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+field+theory"} local
            construction of the derived
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
            is in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            appears “de-transgressed” in the form of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            %em local
            incarnation of the redcuced phase space is modeled by the genuine
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+BV-BRST+complex"} local BV-BRST complex
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalBVBRSTComplexIsDerivedCriticalLocusOfEulerLagrangeForm"}
            below.
          %p
            Finally, under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression+of+variational+differential+forms"} transgression of variational differential forms
            this yields a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            on the graded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+observables"} local observables
            of the field theory. This is the
            %em
              global
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ComplexBVBRSTGlobal"}
            below).
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p#DerivedCriticalLocusInsideLieAlgebroids
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+critical+loci"} derived critical loci
              inside
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroids"} Lie algebroids
          %p
            By analogy with the algebraic formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
            (the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds+into+formal+duals+of+R-algebras"} embedding of Cartesian spaces into formal duals of R-algebras
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AlgebraicFactsOfDifferentialGeometry"}
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroids"} Lie algebroids
          #HomomorphismBetweenLieAlgebroids.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                between
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroids"} Lie algebroids
            %p
              Given two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+Lie+algebroids"} derived Lie algebroids
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}'
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LInfinityAlgebroid"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              between them
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝔞
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝔞
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f \;\colon\; \mathfrak{a} \longrightarrow \mathfrak{a}'
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              between their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
              going the other way around
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟵
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔞
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CE(\mathfrak{a}) \longleftarrow CE(\mathfrak{a}') \;\colon\; f^\ast
            %p such that this covers an algebra homomorphism on the function algebras:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
