                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi S
                        %mo ≃
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X/\mathfrak{g})_{d S \simeq 0}
              in there, as in example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ArchetypeOfBVBRSTComplex"}
            %p
              This issue we discuss in detail in the chapter
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#GaugeFixing"} Gauge fixing
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BVComplexIsHomologicalResolutionPreciselyIfNoNonTrivialImplicitGaugeSymmetres"}
              below.
          %p
            In order to generalize the statement of example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OrdinaryCriticalLocusAsCohomologyOfDerivedCriticalLocus"}
            to the case that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+action"} Lie algebra action
            is taken into account, we need to realize the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+critical+locus"} derived critical locus
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
            of a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
          #DerivedCriticalLocusOfActionLiAlgebroidBicomplexStructure.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+critical+locus"} derived critical locus
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+formalism"} BV-BRST
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicomplex"} bicomplex
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi S
                        %mo ≃
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X/\mathfrak{g})_{d S \simeq 0}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+critical+locus"} derived critical locus
              inside an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+Lie+algebroid"} action Lie algebroid
              as in example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ArchetypeOfBVBRSTComplex"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+differential"} Chevalley-Eilenberg differential
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ExplicitCEDifferentialInCotangentBundleOfActionLieAlgebroid"} (9)
              may be decomposed as the sum of two anti-commuting differential
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
