            %p
              all three terms have to vanish separately, as shown, since they each have different bidegree (the last term denotes the graded commutator, hence the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anticommutator"} anticommutator
            %p
              Notice that the nilpotency of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi BV
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_{BV}
              is also immediately checked explicitly, due to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariance
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              (example
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GaugeInvariantFunctionsIntermsOfLieAlgebroids"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
