          %p
            As a corollary of prop. \refDerivedCriticalLocusOfActionLiAlgebroidBicomplexStructure{} we obtain the generalization of example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OrdinaryCriticalLocusAsCohomologyOfDerivedCriticalLocus"}
            to non-trivial
            = succeed "-actions:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          #CochainCohomologyOfBVBRSTComplexInDegreeZero.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
                in degree 0 is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
                function on the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/critical+locus"} critical locus
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi S
                        %mo ≃
                        %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X/\mathfrak{g})_{d S \simeq 0}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+critical+locus"} derived critical locus
              inside an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+Lie+algebroid"} action Lie algebroid
              as in example
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ArchetypeOfBVBRSTComplex"}
            %p
              Then if the vertical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              (prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DerivedCriticalLocusOfActionLiAlgebroidBicomplexStructure"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi CE
                              %mrow
                                %mo •
                                %mo ,
                                %mo •
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                                %mn 1
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi 𝔤
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mrow
                                  %mi d
                                  %mi S
                                  %mo ≃
