            %a{:href => "local+BRST+cohomology#BarnichHenneaux96"}> Barnich-Henneaux 96 (B.6) and footnote 9
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              That the two expressions differ by a horizontally exact terms follows by the very definition of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+derivative"} Euler-Lagrange derivative
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:EulerLagrangeEquationGeneral"} (?)
            %p
              The third point requires some computation (
              %a{:href => "local+BRST+cohomology#BarnichHenneaux96"}> Barnich-Henneaux 96 (B.9)
              ).
            %p
              Finally that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{-,-\}'
              vanishes when at least one of its arguments is horizontally exact follows from the fact that already the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+derivative"} Euler-Lagrange derivative
              vanishes on this argument (example
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TrivialLagrangianDensities"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{-,-\}
              is horizontally exact when at least one of its arguments is so, by the first item.
          %p
            The following is the local refinement of prop.
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassicalMasterEquation"}
          #ClassicalMasterEquationLocal.num_defn
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (local
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+master+equation"} classical master equation
            %p
              The third item in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BasicPropertiesOfTheLocalAntibracket"}
              implies that the following conditions on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi K
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi T
